  "title": "Ukraine and Russia: Zelensky and Trump's Strategic Tensions",
  "summary": "Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky and U.S. President Donald Trump are set to meet as Zelensky seeks to secure an energy truce while Russia, which invaded Ukraine, has received multiple breaks from the U.S. The two leaders have been at odds over the ongoing conflict and international support for Ukraine.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Ukraine President Volodymyr Zelensky supports a truce between Russia and Ukraine, citing the need for energy supplies.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "U.S. President Donald Trump's announcement of a ceasefire is met with initial optimism from Ukraine but not from Russia.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Ukraine has been targeting Russia's oil industry for months, prompting fuel rationing and Russia's ban on diesel exports.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
