      "description": "US President Donald Trump on Monday told reporters he believes the war in Iran \"militarily is effectively over.\"\nThe president made a surprise visit to the White House briefing room after meeting with Qatar's prime minister earlier in the day.\n\"Iran militarily is effectively over,\" Trump said. \"We're just keeping it the status quo.\"\nTrump added that Iran has been \"decapitated\" but said he is still looking to make sure there's a long-term solution to ensuring that Iran's nuclear programme is defanged.\nThe president offered some of his most definitive comments about moving away from his threat to resume strikes on Iran after the US midterm elections passed.\nThe president's Republican Party lost both chambers of Congress to Democrats in last week's elections. The election was shadowed by dissatisfaction among the American electorate over the eight-month-old war, which has led to a surge in fuel prices that's impacted nearly ever sector of the global economy.\nTrump at his news confer",
